{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1898 patchset 2: fixed a REAL regression the LLM code-review flagged (advisory but genuine). C3a-CORE's cut had routed the reconciler's REBAR_ROOT-unset fallback through config.repo_root() (git-toplevel-of-cwd -> cwd), but every reconciler module's OLD fallback was the deterministic, cwd-independent Path(__file__).parents[4] package root; a reconciler daemon run from any cwd would have leaked the caller's checkout. Added owned resolver config.reconciler_repo_root() (REBAR_ROOT or parents[2]-from-config == parents[4]-from-reconciler, verified equal in source+installed layouts) and pointed all 13 reconciler sites at it. RED-first: added held-out test_reconciler_repo_root_unset_fallback_is_cwd_independent (RED against old code, GREEN after) + test_reconciler_event_identity_env_override_propagates (finding #3 coverage). Oracle now 10 GREEN, gate 0 findings, lint/typecheck clean, regression 2864 passed. Re-pushed patchset 2 (Change-Id preserved). Awaiting fresh LLM-Review+1/Verified+1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787129951654308001,"uuid":"8cf60943-ffc5-4145-866b-7db799f45c78"}